# Draw Top-Level Behavior

Draw a mermaid diagram that shows the top-level behavior.

## Inputs

- A ticket, story, use case, or feature description with acceptance criteria.
- Any prior codebase research.
- A high-level design that defines the current state, future state, decisions made, etc.
- Data definitions that will be added and or changed.

## Instructions
- Create a mermaid diagram that shows the top-level behavior.
- Emit the report itself. Do not wrap it in a code fence: the first line of your reply is the opening `## Top-level Behavior`. The report's top heading is `##`, and every heading inside it is `###` or deeper.

## Workflow

- Read all the inputs FULLY.
- Generate the diagram.
- Report using the report format below.

## Report Format
```md
## Top-level Behavior

### Diagram
<mermaid diagram>

### Summary
<very brief summary of the diagram>
```
